# Chrono Nexus — Dialogue Manager script.
# Stage tags: #bg #sprite #focus #music #sfx #box
# Converted from the Dialogic timelines. Typewriter audio is not used.
using GameState

~ opening
Ren: (The humming of the fluorescent lights... the quiet scratching of chalk... and the rain beating against the classroom windows.) [#bg=classroom, #sprite=ren:left, #sprite=none:right, #focus=left, #music=calm]
Ren: (As a foreign exchange student, I've spent weeks in Tokyo trying to blend into the shadows. Literally and figuratively.)
Ren: (But today, the silence in the old school building feels heavy. The air is vibrating...)
Ren: (Wait. The desks... they're flickering? The chalkboard is folding in on itself!) [#sfx=open]
Ren: (The school is gone. I am floating in a magnificent, terrifying fracture of reality—crystals floating in starlight...) [#bg=nexus, #music=tense]
Aurora: U-Um… system integrity at 84%… The rift waves are making everything feel all tingly and unstable… [#sprite=aurora_serious:right, #focus=right, #tween=right:position=0 -8:1.5:sine:in_out?relative&yoyo&loops=0]
Aurora: W-Wait! A localized foreign signature... Your physical structure is... entirely made of shifting shadows? [#sprite=aurora_surprised:right]
Aurora: S-Stranger…? You just appeared in my classroom dimension. I’m Aurora… the subsystem construct of the Chrono Nexus. But your presence is… making my holographic layers glitch… [#sprite=aurora_blush:right]
Aurora: Your bio-signature is actively resonating with my core! The interference is fading… but why is my outfit phase-stabilizer suddenly flickering so much?! [#sprite=aurora_surprised:right]
Kira: Yahoo~! Don’t hog all the fun, Aurora-chan! My sunfire sensors went crazy from the next dimension over! [#sprite=kira_happy:left, #focus=left, #music=warm]
Kira: Hehe, is this the shadowy traveler everyone’s whispering about? Ren, is it? You look kinda tasty up close~
Aurora: K-Kira! Physical boundary protocols! The traveler’s proximity is making my outfit phases flip! [#sprite=aurora_blush:right, #focus=right]
Kira: Aww, your holographic skirt is flickering again! Let me get reaaally close and check~ [#sprite=kira_blush:left, #focus=left]
Kira: Whoa—! The floor just tilted!

- Step closer to steady Aurora
	do steadied_aurora = true
	do add_bond("aurora", 2)
	do add_trust(1)
	Aurora: Ahh—! Your hand went right through my waist… It feels warm… like my core is melting… [#sprite=aurora_blush:right, #focus=right]
	Aurora: Thank you, Ren... The instability dropped… but now my heart is the one glitching… [#sprite=aurora_happy:right]
	Kira: No fair! I want some of that shadow-traveler warmth too! [#sprite=kira_blush:left]
- Reach toward Kira instead
	do reached_for_kira = true
	do add_bond("kira", 2)
	do add_trust(1)
	Kira: H-Hey! Those glowing eyes are way too intense from this close! My tail’s puffing up! [#sprite=kira_blush:left, #focus=left]
	Kira: Eek—! My skirt just flipped from the rift wind! Don’t look, don't look!
	Aurora: Traveler… please don’t ignore my calibration… It feels lonely when you’re far… [#sprite=aurora_sad:right]
Aurora: L-Look out! The rift is pulling us again! [#bg=rift, #sprite=none:left, #sprite=none:right, #music=tense, #sfx=open, #shake=bg:6:0.9, #shake=stage:4:0.9]
=> sanctum

~ beginning
Ren: (The fluorescent lights hum at sixty hertz. Every second, the same tone. Every second, the same emptiness.) [#bg=classroom, #sprite=none:left, #sprite=none:right, #music=calm]
Ren: (Rain slides in slow, crooked rivers down the window. The chalkboard is a blur of quadratic equations and forgotten names.)
Ren: (I sit at the last desk in the last row. My pen hasn't touched paper in forty minutes.)
Ren: (Airports. Hotels. Transit lounges. I have spent my entire life as a cartographic ghost — a pin on a map that migrates before anyone can circle it.)
Ren: (They shipped me to Tokyo the way they ship freight: with paperwork, insurance, and a forwarding address I will never use. The brochure called it "cultural immersion." I call it exile with a stamp.)
Ren: (Teachers skip my name during roll call. Students walk past my desk as though it were empty. Even the janitor sometimes stacks chairs on top of mine during evening rounds.)
Ren: (I watch the rain. I watch the clock. I watch the shadow my body casts against the wall — thinner than anyone else's.)
Ren: (Even water knows where it belongs. It follows the glass down. It doesn't float.)
Ren: (...)
Ren: (Wait. The clock says 3:47. The classroom is empty. But — something is wrong.)
Ren: (The fluorescent lights just flickered. Not the usual flicker — the color shifted. White bleeding toward electric blue.) [#sfx=open]
Ren: (The chalkboard... the equations have stopped mid-formula. The chalk dust is hanging in the air — each particle spiraling slowly, as though gravity has grown uncertain of its own laws.)
Ren: (The desks closest to the wall are flickering. Not like faulty lights — like a screen resolving a signal. Blurring, sharpening, blurring again.)
Ren: (I'm standing. The chair scraped the floor. The sound was too loud — too present — as if the room was holding its breath and I just broke it.)
Ren: (The rain on the window... it's reversing. The drops are crawling upward.)
Ren: (The wall — the far wall — it's bending inward. Like paper caught in a draft.)
Ren: (Behind it is not the hallway. Not the stairwell. Behind it is...)
Ren: (...crystal.) [#bg=nexus, #music=tense]
Ren: (Towering columns of translucent, star-shot glass hang suspended in a void that has no ceiling and no floor. The light here is not fluorescent — it's the pale glow of dying nebulae filtered through faceted mineral.)
Ren: (The air, if it is air, tastes of ozone and cold iron. The gravity is wrong. My hair is drifting upward. My shoelaces are untying themselves.)
Ren: (The classroom is gone. Just — gone. Snapped shut like a book that decided it was finished being read.)
Ren: (I'm floating. My body feels lighter than it ever has, and also less real. I look down at my hands...) [#sprite=ren:left, #focus=left]
Ren: (...not skin. Not bone. Shadow. A flowing, ink-dark silhouette edged with faint cyan luminescence where my veins used to be.)
Ren: (I should be afraid. Part of me is screaming.)
Ren: (But the rest of me... this impossible fracture of crystal and void — it feels more real than any classroom I've ever sat in.)
Ren: (As though reality has finally stopped pretending to be solid and admitted what I always suspected: the world is a series of overlapping projections, and I just fell through the gaps.)
Ren: "..."
Aurora: U-Um… system integrity at 84%… The rift waves are making everything feel all tingly and unstable… [#sprite=aurora_surprised:right, #focus=right]
Aurora: W-Wait! A localized foreign signature… Your physical structure is… entirely made of shifting shadows?
Aurora: S-Stranger…? You just appeared in my classroom dimension. I'm Aurora… the subsystem construct of the Chrono Nexus. But your presence is… making my holographic layers glitch… [#sprite=aurora_blush:right]
Aurora: Your bio-signature is actively resonating with my core! The interference is fading… but why is my outfit phase-stabilizer suddenly flickering so much?! [#sprite=aurora_surprised:right]
Ren: (She's luminous. A girl composed of translucent, softly flickering light — cool blues and pale whites, like a holographic projection trying its best to look alive.)
Ren: (Her costume is unstable. A ripple passes through the holographic fabric — layers phasing transparent before snapping back. She notices me noticing and flushes a deeper shade of blue.)
Aurora: Your shadow… when it touched me… the instability stopped. My core feels… quiet. I haven't felt quiet since the reactor… [#sprite=aurora_blush:right, #focus=right]
Ren: (She presses both hands against her chest, as though trying to hold herself together. Her holographic layers ripple again — slower, more gently. Like a pond settling after a stone is thrown.)
Ren: (When she looks back at me, her eyes are wide and bright. She's not looking at me with scientific curiosity anymore.)
Ren: (She's looking at me the way someone looks at the first warm thing they have felt in a very long time.)
Aurora: Thank you… I think. Your shadow — it felt warm. Like my core is melting…
Ren: (A crack of energy splits the air above us.) [#sfx=open]
Kira: Yahoo~! Don't hog all the fun, Aurora-chan! My sunfire sensors went crazy from the next dimension over! [#sprite=kira_happy:left, #focus=left, #music=warm]
Kira: Hehe, is this the shadowy traveler everyone's whispering about? Ren, is it? You look kinda tasty up close~
Aurora: K-Kira! Physical boundary protocols! The traveler's proximity is making my outfit phases flip! [#sprite=aurora_blush:right]
Kira: Aww, your holographic skirt is flickering again! Let me get reaaally close and check~ [#sprite=kira_blush:left, #focus=left]
Ren: (She burns. Where Aurora is translucent and gentle, this girl is alive in a way that defies physics. Athletic build, golden hair streaked with amber, cat ears that twitch independently — scanning the space around her like radar dishes.)
Ren: (Her outfit is tactical straps and deliberate exposure. Light armor that bares more skin than it covers, built for speed rather than protection. And she's close enough that the heat radiating from her skin prickles against my cold shadow-form like sunlight on frost.)
Kira: Whoa—! The floor just tilted!

- Step closer to steady Aurora
	do steadied_aurora = true
	do add_bond("aurora", 2)
	do add_trust(1)
	Aurora: Ahh—! Your hand went right through my waist… It feels warm… like my core is melting… [#sprite=aurora_blush:right, #focus=right]
	Aurora: Thank you, Ren... The instability dropped… but now my heart is the one glitching… [#sprite=aurora_happy:right]
	Kira: No fair! I want some of that shadow-traveler warmth too! [#sprite=kira_blush:left]
- Reach toward Kira instead
	do reached_for_kira = true
	do add_bond("kira", 2)
	do add_trust(1)
	Kira: H-Hey! Those glowing eyes are way too intense from this close! My tail's puffing up! [#sprite=kira_blush:left, #focus=left]
	Kira: Eek—! My skirt just flipped from the rift wind! Don't look, don't look!
	Aurora: Traveler… please don't ignore my calibration… It feels lonely when you're far… [#sprite=aurora_sad:right]
Ren: (The Nexus hums around us, ancient and amused — as if testing how close three disparate souls can get before the mathematics of intimacy overwrite the mathematics of physics.)
Ren: (I stand at the center of it, a shadow between two lights, and feel — for the first time in my life — that the void I have carried inside myself might not be emptiness at all.)
Ren: (It might be a space waiting to be filled.)
Aurora: L-Look out! The rift is pulling us again! Crystal pillars are shattering into starlight! [#bg=rift, #music=tense, #sfx=open]
Kira: Grab on, shadow-boy! This ride's about to get rough~ [#sprite=kira_happy:left, #focus=left]
Ren: (Aurora reaches for my hand. Kira grabs my jacket. The Nexus pulls us all downward, sideways, inward — through layers of folded space and fractured memory.)
Ren: (Toward the Starry Sanctum, where two more voices wait in the silence.) [#sprite=none:left, #sprite=none:right]
Ren: (One is soft as moonlight on water.)
Ren: (The other is sharp as a blade wrapped in silk.)
Ren: (And the story, which has only just begun, has already decided it will not let me be invisible anymore.)
=> sanctum

~ sanctum
Ren: You blink hard as the rift spits you out, the classroom fading behind you like a half-remembered dream. Floating crystal pillars drift in soft starlight, and the air feels thick enough to touch. Your pulse hasn’t slowed since the pull began. [#bg=nexus, #sprite=none:left, #sprite=none:right, #music=night]
Ren: (This silence… it’s beautiful, but it presses against my skin like it’s alive. Every breath feels like it’s being watched. And why does it feel like the walls are leaning in closer the longer I stand here?)
Elara: May the starlight guide us… The Nexus has drawn us into a sanctum of pure silence. I am Elara, healer of the moonlit groves. Aurora’s last message spoke of a traveler whose presence could steady the rifts. That must be you. [#sprite=elara_neutral:left, #focus=left]
Elara: Oh—! The moment you arrived the air grew warmer. My healing vestments are already reacting, the silk clinging tighter with every shift in the atmosphere. [#sprite=elara_blush:left]
Ren: (She looks gentle, almost fragile, but there’s a quiet strength in how she holds herself. Still, that blush is spreading fast, and the way the fabric moves with her breathing is… distracting.)
Selene: Quiet indeed, Elara. But with our new guest this sanctuary might become rather... exquisite. I am Selene, keeper of twilight spells. Welcome to the outer sanctums, traveler. Few arrive without panic in their eyes. [#sprite=selene_neutral:right, #focus=right]
Selene: Look at you already fidgeting, Elara. The sheer silk is clinging in all the right ways~ Your cheeks glow brighter than the crystals around us. [#sprite=selene_happy:right]
Elara: S-Selene! Please show some restraint… The rift wind keeps lifting everything again! Traveler, please don’t stare too long… it’s embarrassing when the fabric behaves like this. [#sprite=elara_blush:left, #focus=left]
Selene: Mmm, and your glowing energy is radiating straight toward the traveler. How adorable. I wonder if our guest feels the same pull I do. [#sprite=selene_blush:right]
Ren: (These two already feel like they’ve known each other forever, yet the air between us crackles with something new. Elara’s vestments are nearly translucent at the edges, and Selene’s robe keeps sliding off her shoulder with every little movement. This dimension really doesn’t believe in personal space.)
Elara: The rift energy is making my vestments almost translucent in places… I can feel every shift when you move closer. It’s as if the sanctum itself wants us nearer. [#sprite=elara_blush:left, #focus=left]
Selene: Careful, healer. If you keep blushing like that the traveler might think you want them even nearer. My own robe is already slipping from the unstable gravity here. [#sprite=selene_blush:right, #focus=right]

- Speak softly to Elara while gently steadying her hand
	do comforted_elara = true
	do add_bond("elara", 2)
	do add_insight(1)
	Elara: Your voice… it carries the calming power of ancient lunar waters. My heart is beating so fast it might burst through the silk. [#sprite=elara_happy:left, #focus=left]
	Elara: The fabric is settling… but being this close to you feels even more dangerous than the rift. Your warmth is seeping straight into my core, and I don’t want it to stop. [#sprite=elara_blush:left]
	Kira: (from somewhere distant) No fair! I want some of that traveler warmth too!
- Lean in and trade teasing remarks with Selene
	do teased_selene = true
	do add_bond("selene", 2)
	do add_insight(1)
	Selene: A sharp mind to match a daring presence. I like that very much. Most travelers panic the moment they arrive here, yet you meet our eyes so steadily. [#sprite=selene_happy:right, #focus=right]
	Selene: Perhaps you'd like to study my spellbooks under closer illumination? My robe might slip if you lean in any more~ The rift wind loves to play with loose fabric, and I’m starting to enjoy the game. [#sprite=selene_blush:right]
	Elara: Traveler… don’t forget about my core calibration. It feels lonely when you’re too far. The silence here makes every little touch echo like a promise. [#sprite=elara_sad:left]
Ren: (Both of them are getting more flustered by the second. The way their outfits keep reacting to the air, the soft blushes, the charged glances… this place mixes beauty with something almost scary. Like the dimension itself is gently pushing us together, testing how close we’ll allow ourselves to become.)
Selene: The fabric of our universe is complex… but these moments of connection feel perfectly simple. And dangerously intimate. The Nexus seems to enjoy watching us grow closer, peeling away the distance one heartbeat at a time. [#sprite=selene_neutral:right, #focus=right]
Elara: Please… let’s not let the silence turn into something we can’t control. Though your eyes are making it very hard to focus on the rift. [#sprite=elara_blush:left]
Elara: Ah—! The sanctum is destabilizing again! The wind is picking up… I can feel my vestments lifting! [#bg=rift, #music=tense, #sfx=open]
Selene: Traveler, stay close! The rift is pulling us toward the next sanctum. This is only the beginning of the Nexus’s games with our hearts. [#sprite=selene_surprised:right, #focus=right]
Ren: (My thoughts are spinning. These girls, this place, the way everything feels so charged and fragile at once… I have a feeling the Chrono Nexus isn’t going to let me stay distant for long. Every glance, every accidental closeness, is starting to feel like the real adventure.) [#sprite=none:left, #sprite=none:right]
=> grove

~ grove
The rift settles you into the moonlit grove where glowing leaves drift like slow fireflies. Towering trees twist into impossible arches overhead, their branches whispering secrets in a language that makes your chest tighten. The air is cool but charged, carrying the faint scent of blossoms that seem to bloom only when you look away. [#bg=grove, #sprite=none:left, #sprite=none:right, #music=night]
Ren: [i]This place… it’s like the silence from the sanctum followed us here, but now it’s breathing through the trees. Every shadow feels like it’s leaning in to watch.[/i]
Kira: Yahoo~! Finally caught up with you, traveler! The rift dragged me through three dimensions just to get here. I’m Kira, by the way—sunfire catgirl and professional trouble magnet. You must be Ren, right? Aurora’s been mumbling your name through the static. [#sprite=kira_happy:right, #focus=right]
Kira: Hehe, you look even cuter up close than the rift visions showed. My ears are already twitching just from standing this near.
The leaves rustle without wind, brushing against Kira’s short skirt and making the tactical straps on her outfit shift teasingly. A low, distant sound echoes from deeper in the grove, sending a soft shiver up your spine.
Ren: [i]Kira’s energy is infectious, but that sound… it reminds me the Nexus isn’t just playing matchmaker. Something might be moving between the trees.[/i]
Kira: Whoa—did you feel that? The grove’s wind just flipped my skirt again! Don’t look… or do, I guess? My tail’s all puffed up from the tension. [#sprite=kira_blush:right]
Aurora: Ren… the resonance between us is stronger here. My holographic layers keep glitching whenever you’re close. I am Aurora, the subsystem construct. The whispers in these leaves… they’re fragments of old memories trying to pull us into something intimate and terrifying at once. [#sprite=aurora_serious:left, #focus=left]
Aurora: The fabric of my outfit is phasing again… it’s like the grove wants you to see how vulnerable I really am. [#sprite=aurora_blush:left]
The distant sound grows softer, almost playful, as glowing petals drift between you and the girls. Kira steps closer on instinct, her shoulder brushing yours in a way that sends warmth straight through your jacket. The leaves continue their gentle dance, creating a calm rhythm that lets the three of you simply stand together, breathing the same charged air. Aurora’s form flickers softly with each passing petal, while Kira’s ears twitch in time with the whispers, her playful energy settling into a quieter warmth. The grove seems to pause, giving space for the moment to stretch, letting the closeness build without urgency. Your thoughts drift to how these girls have already started to feel familiar, their blushes and small reactions turning the strange dimension into something almost tender.
Ren: [i]Every glance, every accidental touch… the Nexus is turning fear into something warmer, but that sound reminds me we’re not alone in here. Still, their blushes and the way their outfits keep betraying them make it hard to pull away.[/i]
Kira: The whispers say the next sanctum is calling. But staying here a little longer… with you… feels like the real adventure starting. [#sprite=kira_happy:right, #focus=right]
Aurora: Ren, whatever happens next, remember these moments. The grove is watching, and it loves when we let the tension build. [#sprite=aurora_happy:left, #focus=left]
=> shore

~ shore
Ren: The rift currents release us with a gentle, warm breath of air. The cold starlight of the sanctuary is replaced by a vast, glowing sunset over an endless, surreal sea. [#bg=shore, #sprite=none:left, #sprite=none:right, #music=warm]
Elara: The Nexus has guided us to the Shore of Whispers... The tide here carries the memories of civilizations long before the rifts began. [#sprite=elara_neutral:left, #focus=left]
Selene: A beach at sunset... How incredibly cliché of this dimension. Yet, under this light, the way the waves reflect off your shadow-cloak, Ren, is quite beautiful. [#sprite=selene_neutral:right, #focus=right]
Elara: Selene! Please... the tropical warm front is already making my healing robes cling. The salt air makes the fabric so heavy... and translucent. [#sprite=elara_blush:left, #focus=left]
Selene: Oh, my dear healer. If the traveler didn't want to look, they would have turned their glowing eyes away by now. Look at how they watch you. [#sprite=selene_happy:right]

- Comfort Elara and adjust her shawl
	do comforted_elara = true
	do add_bond("elara", 1)
	do add_trust(1)
	Elara: A-Ah... your shadow-touch is surprisingly cool against the salt heat. Thank you... [#sprite=elara_blush:left, #focus=left]
	Elara: My heart... the waves are whispering of ancient bonds. Being near you makes me feel so safe. [#sprite=elara_happy:left]
	Selene: My, how tender. Perhaps I should feel a bit jealous? [#sprite=selene_blush:right]
- Stand with Selene and watch the tide
	do teased_selene = true
	do add_bond("selene", 1)
	do add_trust(1)
	Selene: The horizon seems to stretch into infinity, doesn't it? But with you standing next to me, Ren, the infinite feels perfectly within reach. [#sprite=selene_happy:right, #focus=right]
	Selene: Look, a warm breeze is picking up. My twilight robes aren't built for ocean winds... see how they sway? [#sprite=selene_blush:right]
	Elara: S-Selene! You're letting the wind pull your shoulder straps down on purpose! [#sprite=elara_blush:left]
Selene: Closeness in the Nexus is never accidental. The dimensions shape themselves around what our souls desire most. [#sprite=selene_neutral:right, #focus=right]
Elara: Let's continue forward before the tide rises too high. The path ahead is leading into the core of the Nexus itself. [#sprite=elara_blush:left, #focus=left]
The tide draws back, and the path under it is made of light. [#bg=core, #sprite=none:left, #sprite=none:right, #music=tense]
=> core

~ core
Ren: The core of the Chrono Nexus. A massive sphere of rotating crystal, humming with the raw power of space and time. [#bg=core, #sprite=none:left, #sprite=none:right, #music=tense]
Aurora: Ren... you came back to me. The subsystem matrices are completely synchronized now. [#sprite=aurora_gorgeous:right, #focus=right]
Aurora: Look at the crystal... it's mirroring your shadow form, wrapping us both in a soft, twilight glow. [#sprite=aurora_blush:right]
Kira: I told you we'd make it! The sunfire power is at maximum! [#sprite=kira_happy:left, #focus=left]
Elara: The rifts are calm. The light from the core feels warm and welcoming. [#sprite=elara_happy:left, #focus=left]
Selene: And look at us... gathered at the heart of existence itself. Quite a romantic view for a shadowy foreign exchange student, don't you think? [#sprite=selene_happy:right, #focus=right]
Aurora: Ren... as long as you are with us, the Nexus will never fracture again. Our souls are woven together, across every horizon, across every lifetime. [#sprite=aurora_gorgeous:right, #focus=right]
Ren: (The warmth of their presence, the soft blushes, the memories we've forged... the Chrono Nexus is no longer a prison. It is our sanctuary.) [#bg=festival, #sprite=none:left, #sprite=none:right, #music=loop:night]
=> opening

~ lab
Ren: Что же мне сделать дальше? Квантовые флуктуации вокруг нарастают... [#bg=lab, #sprite=ren:left, #sprite=none:right, #focus=left, #music=tense]

- Поддержать Аврору
	do supported_aurora = true
	do add_bond("aurora", 2)
	do add_trust(1)
	Ren: (Рен делает шаг вперед, берет Аврору за руку, чтобы помочь ей справиться со сбоем, и тепло смотрит на Киру и Селену.)
	Aurora: — Спасибо, Рен… Мне уже… уже чуть лучше. Просто… иногда всё начинает мерцать и расплываться, и я… я теряюсь. Но с тобой… с тобой я чувствую себя в безопасности. [#sprite=aurora_blush:right, #focus=right]
	Kira: — Ой‑ой, какая милота, прям сахарные облака и радужные единороги! Может, вы ещё и в хоровод возьмётесь? А то я тут чуть не растаяла от всей этой… нежности. *[лёгкий сбой в ткани куртки — рукав на мгновение мерцает и искажается, прежде чем вернуться в нормальное состояние]* [#sprite=kira_happy:right]
	Selene: — Милота, говоришь? Пожалуй, в чём‑то ты права, Кира. Но знаешь, что ещё интереснее? То, как мир вокруг нас слегка… плывёт. Видишь эти глитчи? Одежда мерцает, воздух дрожит — словно сама реальность даёт сбой. И всё это, заметь, началось не так давно… примерно с тех пор, как появился *он*. Любопытно, не находишь? *[лёгкое движение рукой — край плаща на мгновение теряет чёткие очертания, расплывается туманной дымкой, затем вновь обретает форму]* [#sprite=selene_happy:right, #focus=right]
- Защитить Нову в темноте
	do protected_nova = true
	do add_bond("nova", 2)
	do add_bond("aria", 1)
	do add_power(1)
	Ren: (Внезапно реактор отключается. Рен окутывает дрожащую Нову своей тенью и зовет Арию.) [#sfx=error]
	Aria: «Рен! Я здесь! Держитесь — я иду к вам!» *Перья осыпаются искрами, мерцая в густом озоновом воздухе, контуры фигуры слегка размываются из‑за сбоев в локальной гравитации.* [#sprite=aria_surprised:right, #focus=right]
	Elara: «Рен… Я здесь. Дайте мне помочь — я целительница, я обязана быть рядом в час беды…» *Лёгкая ткань моего одеяния слегка мерцает и местами будто растворяется в воздухе из‑за сбоев в гравитации, контуры рукавов размываются, но я стараюсь держаться ровно, сосредоточившись на том, чтобы подойти ближе.* [#sprite=elara_neutral:right]
The reactor hum falls back into a heartbeat. For one breath, the lab remembers how to be a room. [#sprite=none:left, #sprite=none:right, #music=calm]
=> END
